{
  "milestoneId": "M001",
  "sliceId": "S02",
  "sliceTitle": "Scroll Choreography and Reduced Motion",
  "oneLiner": "Centralized Lenis and GSAP scroll choreography now drives the editorial shell, with reduced-motion guards and tests keeping all sections static and readable when motion is disabled.",
  "narrative": "S02 added a contained `useEditorialMotion` hook that owns all Lenis and GSAP ScrollTrigger integration for the redesigned portfolio. The hook registers ScrollTrigger, initializes Lenis only when `prefers-reduced-motion` is not active, proxies Lenis scroll state into ScrollTrigger, sets an inspectable `data-reduced-motion` attribute on the document element, and cleans up timelines, triggers, RAF handles, and Lenis state on unmount. The editorial page now consumes that hook at the shell level and exposes stable `data-motion-*` hooks on the opening identity, section reveal groups, selected-work spread, and timeline year placeholders so later content inherits the choreography instead of reimplementing it. CSS was adjusted so pre-JS and reduced-motion states remain visible and readable rather than depending on hidden-until-animated content. The test environment was also hardened for motion code: Jest maps Lenis and GSAP to test-compatible modules, a global matchMedia stub is installed before module load, and the focused motion test suite verifies reduced-motion behavior and normal motion initialization.",
  "verification": "Fresh closeout verification passed. `npm run build` and `npm test -- --watchAll=false --testPathPattern=editorial-motion --forceExit` were run through `gsd_exec` in run e97d0735-2aab-4fca-9802-6eb3e442b8d8; both exited 0. A local CRA dev server was started and a headless Microsoft Edge CDP scroll check navigated to `http://localhost:3000`, scrolled through the page, and reported `browser_console_errors=0` in `gsd_exec` run 35be60de-e3a7-47a9-af1a-493c0c92b034. The initial bash and Playwright attempts failed because the verification environment lacked `/bin/bash` and the `playwright` package; those were tool/environment failures and were superseded by successful Node/Edge verification.",
  "uatContent": "# S02 UAT: Scroll Choreography and Reduced Motion\n\n## UAT Type\nManual browser acceptance with automated build/test evidence.\n\n## Preconditions\n- Dependencies are installed with `npm install`.\n- The app can run locally with `npm start`.\n- Use a modern browser such as Edge or Chrome.\n\n## Steps\n1. Start the site with `npm start` and open `http://localhost:3000`.\n2. Confirm the page opens on the warm cream editorial homepage and the opening identity is visible without waiting for user interaction.\n3. Scroll down through the opening, lede, selected-work placeholder, experience/timeline placeholder, and later editorial sections.\n4. Confirm sections remain readable while moving with smooth scroll pacing and reveal choreography; content should not flicker, disappear permanently, or require a refresh to appear.\n5. Open browser developer tools and confirm no console errors appear during initial load or while scrolling.\n6. Enable OS/browser reduced-motion preference (`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`) and reload the page.\n7. Confirm scrolling becomes static/native, pinned or transformed choreography is disabled, and the same content remains readable in normal document flow.\n8. Inspect the `<html>` element and confirm the reduced-motion state is reflected through the motion state attribute when reduced motion is active.\n\n## Expected Outcomes\n- Normal mode uses Lenis/GSAP choreography on the actual editorial shell sections.\n- Reduced-motion mode does not initialize smooth-scroll or scroll-trigger animation behavior.\n- All major sections remain visible before JS animation runs and after cleanup/reload.\n- The browser console has no app errors during scroll.\n- `npm run build` passes.\n- The focused editorial motion test suite passes.\n\n## Edge Cases\n- If JavaScript loads slowly, content should still be visible rather than hidden by initial animation CSS.\n- If reduced-motion preference is toggled before load, the hook should skip Lenis and ScrollTrigger timelines.\n- If motion initialization fails in development, the failure should surface as a non-secret console error rather than silently breaking the page.\n\n## Not Proven By This UAT\n- Final production copy and CV traceability; those are covered by S03.\n- Build-time GitHub activity fetching and dashboard rendering; those are covered by S04.\n- Full-site final polish and deployment readiness; those are covered by S06.",
